corepack enable
corepack prepare yarn@4.12.0 --activate

### NPM Private Repo Access

Login to npm with your scope:

yarn npm login --scope your-org

This creates `~/.yarnrc.yml` with your auth token.

## Migration Checklist
- [ ] Add `packageManager` field to `package.json`
- [ ] Create/update `.yarnrc.yml` (remove `yarnPath` if present, remove `npmAuthToken`)
- [ ] Update `.gitignore` (remove `!.yarn/releases` exception)
- [ ] Delete `.yarn/releases/` directory if it exists
- [ ] Update Dockerfile to use corepack
- [ ] Update GitHub Actions to use corepack
- [ ] Fix any scripts with unbound environment variables (use `${VAR:-}` syntax)
- [ ] Update README with new setup instructions
- [ ] Run `yarn install` to generate new `yarn.lock`
- [ ] Test locally
- [ ] Test CI/CD pipeline

## Common Issues

### "Package not found" errors
- Ensure you're logged in: `yarn npm login --scope your-org`
- Check `~/.yarnrc.yml` has the correct registry URL

### Environment variable errors
- Use `${VAR:-}` or `${VAR:-default}` for optional env vars
- Yarn 4 doesn't tolerate unset variables in `${VAR}` syntax

### SSL issues locally
- Use environment variable: `NO_TLS=1 yarn dev`
- Do NOT edit `.yarnrc.yml` with `enableStrictSsl: false` (this is a tracked file)

### Corepack not found
- Ensure Node.js 16.10+ is installed
- Run `corepack enable` (may need sudo on some systems)
